<DocsLayout title="Chudware documentation" description="Choose an access path, build your first part, and move through modeling, reverse engineering, collaboration, and manufacturing with practical guides." section="Start here">
  <h2>Build something real</h2>
  <p>These guides follow the shape of an engineering project: choose browser or desktop access, create constrained geometry, assemble parts, rebuild from source evidence, prepare manufacturing work, and keep the project traceable.</p>
  <p>If this is your first session, choose the <a href="/docs/install-windows/">Windows desktop preview</a>, <a href="/docs/install-linux/">Linux desktop preview</a>, or <a href="/docs/install-macos/">macOS browser guide</a>, then continue to <a href="/docs/first-part/">your first part</a>.</p>
  <h2>Rebuild from source evidence</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/docs/reverse-engineering/">reverse engineering guide</a> covers photos, video, scan meshes, datasheets, and library records, with explicit scale confirmation, dimension review, approximate-result labels, deviation, and provenance.</p>
  <h2>Use the copilot as a collaborator</h2>
  <p>The AI copilot can inspect and change the open design, but it does not replace engineering judgment. Review the feature tree, measurements, and highlighted changes before accepting the result.</p>
  <h2>Keep help close</h2>
  <p>Use the documentation menu to move between guides. Search runs entirely in your browser against a static index shipped with this site; your query is not sent to a search provider.</p>
</DocsLayout>
